course: dictionary
lesson: 2838
title: Short words with big meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words are shortened, like «DJ». A shortened word is called an abbreviation. You can work out what it means from the words around it. The sentence below is about a party, with food, dancing and music, so the clues point to what a DJ does.
explain: «In Newcastle, Nan turns 70 and there are 40 relatives, a DJ, a buffet with sausage rolls stacked like bricks, and Uncle Gaz doing the Macarena.» A buffet and a dance like the Macarena tell you this is a party. So a DJ must be the person who plays the music.
explain: The same word can work as different parts of speech. A DJ is a person, a noun. To DJ is a verb: it means to be the DJ at an event. Look at how the word is used in the sentence to decide which one it is.
fact: DJ is short for disc jockey.
fact: A DJ is a person who plays recorded music at a party, club or on the radio.
fact: DJ can also be a verb. To DJ means to be the DJ at an event.
fact: Informal means relaxed, everyday language, the sort used with friends rather than in formal writing.
fact: In older UK use, DJ can stand for dinner jacket, a smart black jacket worn at formal events.
exercise: «In Newcastle, Nan turns 70 and there are 40 relatives, a DJ, a buffet...» What is a DJ at a party? | Food served on sticks | A dance step | *A person who plays recorded music | A relative of Nan
exercise: DJ is short for which words? | dear juice | dinner joke | *disc jockey | dance jump
exercise: In «Mum will DJ the school disco», what kind of word is DJ? | A noun, meaning a thing | A pronoun, standing in for a name | *A verb, meaning to play music at an event | An adjective, describing the disco
test: Where might you hear a radio DJ? | Under the sea | *On the radio, playing music for listeners | In a bakery, selling bread | At the dentist
test: In «Dad and I will DJ the wedding», what does DJ mean? | To send the invitations | *To be the DJ and play music at the wedding | To take the photos | To cook the wedding food
exam: On an old invitation it says «Black tie, DJ», so what does DJ most likely stand for? | dance jam | disc jockey | *dinner jacket | dog jumper
